  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The tangent line approximation of $S(t)$ at the point $a=6$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t) & =S(a)+{S}^{′}(a)(t-a) \\\\  & =S(6)+{S}^{′}(6)(t-6) \\\\  & =4+2(t-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $S(7)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $t=7.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(7) & ≈L(7) \\\\  & =4+2(7-6) \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
